IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cbca-core-definitions`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part I (the rest of it): section 3 (application)
-- and section 4 (purposes). Section 1 (the short title) and the title block are inert; see NOTES.md.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Section 2 and 2.1 (interpretation) are the keel's.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Each rule is named `<what it decides> within s <section>`. A rule that says an
-- act is forbidden or permitted returns TRUE when the forbidding or the permission is the answer for
-- the facts it is given, and the name says which. Judgements the Act hands to someone else, and facts
-- that turn on a document outside the sources, are plain inputs named for the fact.

§ `Part I -- Application`

§§ `s 3(1) to whom the Act applies`

-- "applies to every corporation incorporated and every body corporate continued as a corporation under
-- this Act that has not been discontinued under this Act". That is the keel's definition of
-- "corporation" (s 2(1)), so the rule calls it: it adds nothing of its own.
-- src:116 | Application of Act
-- src:117 | 3 (1) This Act applies to every corporation incorporated and every body corporate continued as a corporation under this Act that has not been discontinued under this Act.
@ref CBCA s 3(1) application of Act (src:116-117)
GIVEN `the corporation was incorporated under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate was continued as a corporation under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate has been discontinued under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`this Act applies to the body corporate within s 3(1)` MEANS
    `corporation within s 2(1)`
        TRUE
        (`the corporation was incorporated under this Act` OR `the body corporate was continued as a corporation under this Act`)
        `the body corporate has been discontinued under this Act`

§§ `s 3(3) Acts that do not apply to a corporation`

-- Paragraph (a) is repealed in this text (src:121); the remaining three are the Canada Not-for-profit
-- Corporations Act, the Winding-up and Restructuring Act, and any provision of a Special Act (as defined
-- in section 87 of the Canada Transportation Act, which is not among the sources) that is inconsistent
-- with this Act. Whether a provision is inconsistent is a judgement for the person asking.
-- src:119 | Certain Acts do not apply
-- src:120 | (3) The following do not apply to a corporation:
-- src:121 | (a) [Repealed, 2009, c. 23, s. 344]
-- src:122 | (a.1) the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act;
-- src:123 | (b) the Winding-up and Restructuring Act; and
-- src:124 | (c) the provisions of a Special Act, as defined in section 87 of the Canada Transportation Act, that are inconsistent with this Act.
@ref CBCA s 3(3) certain Acts do not apply (src:119-124)
DECLARE `Law that s 3(3) may exclude from applying to a corporation` IS ONE OF
    `the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act`
    `the Winding-up and Restructuring Act`
    `a provision of a Special Act, as defined in section 87 of the Canada Transportation Act`
    `any other law`

-- src:119 | Certain Acts do not apply
-- src:120 | (3) The following do not apply to a corporation:
-- src:121 | (a) [Repealed, 2009, c. 23, s. 344]
-- src:122 | (a.1) the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act;
-- src:123 | (b) the Winding-up and Restructuring Act; and
-- src:124 | (c) the provisions of a Special Act, as defined in section 87 of the Canada Transportation Act, that are inconsistent with this Act.
@ref CBCA s 3(3) certain Acts do not apply (src:119-124)
GIVEN `the law` IS A `Law that s 3(3) may exclude from applying to a corporation`
      `the provision of the Special Act is inconsistent with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 87 of the Canada Transportation Act (outside the Act)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the law is excluded from applying to a corporation within s 3(3)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the law`
    WHEN `the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Winding-up and Restructuring Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a provision of a Special Act, as defined in section 87 of the Canada Transportation Act` THEN `the provision of the Special Act is inconsistent with this Act`
    WHEN `any other law` THEN FALSE

§§ `s 3(4) and s 3(5) business a corporation may not carry on`

-- s 3(4): "No corporation shall carry on the business of" a bank, a Cooperative Credit Associations Act
-- association, an Insurance Companies Act company or society, or a Trust and Loan Companies Act company.
-- The four statutes are not among the sources, so which business a person carries on is asked as a fact.
-- src:125 | Limitations on business that may be carried on
-- src:126 | (4) No corporation shall carry on the business of
-- src:127 | (a) a bank;
-- src:128 | (a.1) an association to which the Cooperative Credit Associations Act applies;
-- src:129 | (b) a company or society to which the Insurance Companies Act applies; or
-- src:130 | (c) a company to which the Trust and Loan Companies Act applies.
@ref CBCA s 3(4) limitations on business that may be carried on (src:125-130)
DECLARE `Business a corporation may not carry on under s 3(4)` IS ONE OF
    `the business of a bank`
    `the business of an association to which the Cooperative Credit Associations Act applies`
    `the business of a company or society to which the Insurance Companies Act applies`
    `the business of a company to which the Trust and Loan Companies Act applies`
    `any other business`

-- src:125 | Limitations on business that may be carried on
-- src:126 | (4) No corporation shall carry on the business of
-- src:127 | (a) a bank;
-- src:128 | (a.1) an association to which the Cooperative Credit Associations Act applies;
-- src:129 | (b) a company or society to which the Insurance Companies Act applies; or
-- src:130 | (c) a company to which the Trust and Loan Companies Act applies.
@ref CBCA s 3(4) limitations on business that may be carried on (src:125-130)
GIVEN `the business` IS A `Business a corporation may not carry on under s 3(4)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation is prohibited from carrying on the business within s 3(4)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the business`
    WHEN `the business of a bank` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the business of an association to which the Cooperative Credit Associations Act applies` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the business of a company or society to which the Insurance Companies Act applies` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the business of a company to which the Trust and Loan Companies Act applies` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other business` THEN FALSE

-- s 3(5): a degree-granting educational institution may be carried on only with express authorization
-- by "a federal or provincial agent that by law has the power to confer degree-granting authority".
-- src:131 | Limitations on business that may be carried on
-- src:132 | (5) No corporation shall carry on business as a degree-granting educational institution unless expressly authorized to do so by a federal or provincial agent that by law has the power to confer degree-granting authority on an educational institution.
@ref CBCA s 3(5) limitations on business that may be carried on (src:131-132)
GIVEN `the business is that of a degree-granting educational institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is expressly authorized by a federal or provincial agent that by law has the power to confer degree-granting authority on an educational institution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation is prohibited from carrying on a degree-granting educational institution within s 3(5)` MEANS
        `the business is that of a degree-granting educational institution`
    AND (NOT `the corporation is expressly authorized by a federal or provincial agent that by law has the power to confer degree-granting authority on an educational institution`)

§§ `s 4 purposes of the Act`

-- A purpose clause decides nothing for a person by itself and states no obligation; it is carried as data
-- so that the three purposes are quotable and so that a reader can ask whether a given aim is one of them.
-- The word "transferance" is the text's own spelling.
-- src:135 | Purposes
-- src:136 | 4 The purposes of this Act are to revise and reform the law applicable to business corporations incorporated to carry on business throughout Canada, to advance the cause of uniformity of business corporation law in Canada and to provide a means of allowing an orderly transferance of certain federal companies incorporated under various Acts of Parliament to this Act.
@ref CBCA s 4 purposes (src:135-136)
DECLARE `Purpose of the Act (s 4)` IS ONE OF
    `to revise and reform the law applicable to business corporations incorporated to carry on business throughout Canada`
    `to advance the cause of uniformity of business corporation law in Canada`
    `to provide a means of allowing an orderly transferance of certain federal companies incorporated under various Acts of Parliament to this Act`

-- src:135 | Purposes
-- src:136 | 4 The purposes of this Act are to revise and reform the law applicable to business corporations incorporated to carry on business throughout Canada, to advance the cause of uniformity of business corporation law in Canada and to provide a means of allowing an orderly transferance of certain federal companies incorporated under various Acts of Parliament to this Act.
@ref CBCA s 4 purposes (src:135-136)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Purpose of the Act (s 4)`
`the purposes of this Act within s 4` MEANS
    LIST `to revise and reform the law applicable to business corporations incorporated to carry on business throughout Canada`,
         `to advance the cause of uniformity of business corporation law in Canada`,
         `to provide a means of allowing an orderly transferance of certain federal companies incorporated under various Acts of Parliament to this Act`
